      "Few claim statuses are as vague as \"pending medical review.\" It tells you the claim is not paid and not denied, but not much else. Understanding what is happening behind that status, and what you can do about it, helps you avoid letting these claims age into problems.",
      "## What the status means",
      "A claim pending medical review has been pulled out of automated processing so that a clinical reviewer, such as a nurse or physician, can examine it. The payer wants to confirm that the service was medically necessary, coded correctly, and supported by documentation. Until that review is complete, the claim sits in a suspended state.",
      "Sometimes the payer already has what it needs and the review simply takes time. Often, though, the payer has requested records and is waiting for them. That request may have gone out by mail, fax, or through a portal, and it may not have reached the right person in your office.",
